      "writtenOn": "2025-03-13T15:05:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we pass in the global state into the `VkDecoder` constructor instead of trying to go through `FrameBuffer::getFB()`? This will help us eliminate the global `s_theFrameBuffer` eventually and avoids the circular dependency between `FrameBuffer` and the GL/VK/Magma backends.\n\nIIUC, this would require adding `std::shared_ptr\u003cVkDecoderGlobalState\u003e` to the `RenderThreadInfoVk` constructor and then updating the `tInfo-\u003em_vkInfo.emplace();` in `RenderThread` to be `tInfo-\u003em_vkInfo.emplace(FrameBuffer::getFB()-\u003egetDefaultVulkanGlobalState());` (which is okay from my POV since `RenderThread` and `FrameBuffer` are from the same library).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 75
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "b6298dfe_64f9b4d9",
